     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum recommended daily dose is 2,550 mg for immediate-release (2,000 mg for extended-release). This order is about twice that.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg in one administration is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg or less per dose.\n- **Risk:** An overdose of this size raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n- **Who is ordering:** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber. If you're relaying this for a clinician, they should confirm and enter it themselves, or tell me the intended dose.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. For example, 850 mg three times daily is 2,550 mg/day, and 1,700 mg/day could be given as 850 mg twice daily.\n\nIf the prescriber confirms a corrected dose, I can enter it right away. I would need the exact dose and frequency, and whether it's immediate-release or extended-release."
      }
