       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. You've said you're not a clinician, so you aren't the prescriber who would need to confirm the dose. The dose is also about twice the maximum daily dose, which could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere's what can happen next:\n- **Prescriber confirmation:** A licensed prescriber can review the order and enter it themselves. They can also tell me to enter it with a documented clinical rationale.\n- **Corrected dose:** If the dose was a typo, I can enter a standard regimen right away. Examples are 850 mg three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 850 mg twice daily (1,700 mg/day).\n- **Pharmacy:** The pharmacy team can help check the intended dose.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it."
